Part VI -- epoch-count confound, resolved analytically

cfg.epochs_fast          = 12
cfg.min_epochs_warm_start = 20
early stopping can fire only once ep+1 >= 20, which never happens within 12 epochs -> impossible by construction

best_epoch (which of the guaranteed-run epochs had the lowest val loss) per arm:
         mean   std  min  max  count
variant                             
all3     10.2  0.84    9   11      5
epi       8.4  3.29    3   11      5
seq       5.8  2.77    3    9      5
seq_epi   8.6  2.61    5   11      5
seq_str   8.2  1.30    6    9      5
str      10.0  1.73    7   11      5
str_epi   8.8  2.17    6   11      5

all3 best_epoch:    10.2 +/- 0.7
str_epi best_epoch: 8.8 +/- 1.9
paired p = 0.2635 -- indistinguishable, not the order-of-magnitude gap v1 found

Conclusion: for THIS (warm-started, fast-mode) result, the training-dynamics
confound v1 raised does not apply -- both arms trained the same guaranteed
epoch budget. The H4 significance result (Table V / Section VI.C of the
manuscript) stands on architectural grounds, not on an epoch-count artefact.
This does not extend automatically to a from-scratch (non-warm-started) or
full-scale run, where min_epochs_warm_start does not apply the same way --
state that scope explicitly if this notebook's result is cited for those.
