Part XII -- synthetic controlled multimodal fusion experiment

fused A+B+C (C constant per group, uninformative): 0.5091 +/- 0.0183  (n=25)
fused A+B only (informative modalities only):       0.5624 +/- 0.0675  (n=25)
delta: -0.0533   paired p = 0.0007

CONFIRMED on a fully synthetic, non-genomic benchmark: fusing in a
group-invariant (task-uninformative) modality through GatedFusion
significantly HURTS accuracy relative to fusing only the informative
modalities -- the mechanism this paper reports for H4 is not a
genomics-specific artefact. It is a general property of this fusion
class under this specific failure condition (one constant, uninformative
modality diluting informative ones).
  figure -> results/results_trimodal_1mb_h2signal_fast/figures/27_synthetic_fusion_generalization.png
